<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jan van Swieten</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1807–1888</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jan van Swieten was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> general who commanded the second expedition against the Aceh Sultanate in 1873–1874, after the first had failed and its commander Köhler had been killed. His force captured the sultan's palace in January 1874, and he declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>, but Acehnese resistance continued for three decades.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jan-van-swieten.jpg" alt="Jan van Swieten" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: nvt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swieten,-J-van2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
